# Architecture & UDF Standards
Refer to SSOT: `.shared-rules/01-architecture-udf.md`

- **UiState:** Model as a single sealed interface (`Loading`, `Success`, `Error`). Never expose multiple mutable StateFlows from a ViewModel.
- **State Production:** Always use `.stateIn(scope = viewModelScope, started = SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5_000), initialValue = ...)`.
- **Intents/Effects:** User actions must pass through sealed `UiIntent`. One-off events (navigation, snackbars) must use a buffered `Channel<UiEffect>` exposed as a `Flow`.
- **Layer Boundary:** UI layers must never import or reference Data/DTO classes directly; always map through Domain Models.
